**JavaScript (Node):**
```javascript
const cache = new Map();
const TTL = 5 * 60 * 1000; // 5 min

async function getUserProfile(userId) {
  if (cache.has(userId) && Date.now() - cache.get(userId).time < TTL) {
    return cache.get(userId).data;
  }
  const data = await db.query(userId);
  cache.set(userId, { data, time: Date.now() });
  return data;
}
```

**Better:** set HTTP cache headers and let the browser/CDN handle it—costs zero code.

